experiment: tutorchain
  instrument        tutorchain   trial seed 0000000001355b87   1214 trials per generation
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  tutorchain -- `tutor` showed one creature teaching another at 5.3 SE and
  the distinction narrowing +96.1 -> +25.6 Hz. Does it reach zero, or settle?
  the question  a DECAY and a CONVENTION look identical after one step and
                mean opposite things. Four steps separate them.
  the quantity  dF1 per generation with its own SE, and the ratio of SUMS at
                each step with a jackknife SE -- one denominator per step,
                never a mean of per-creature ratios.
  the control   `flip` exchanges the labels at EVERY step, so if transmission
                is real the sign must ALTERNATE: -, +, -, + for generations
                1 to 4. A POSITIVE prediction, much harder to hit by accident
                than a null, and it also shows the chain carries information
                rather than drifting.
  the bars      fixed before the run. DECAY if generation 4 is within 3 SE of
                zero. CONVENTION if generation 4 clears 3 SE and generations
                2-4 agree within 3 SE of their own mean. Anything else is
                STILL FALLING and is reported as that, with no rate fitted.
  18 chains, 5 generations deep, two chains per creature.


  generation   faithful chain dF1       flipped chain dF1        lesson drop (faithful)
  0             +96.1 +/-   5.1 Hz      (shared with faithful)   +0.1480 +/- 0.0053    
  1             +25.6 +/-   7.6 Hz       -27.7 +/-   6.5 Hz      +0.0531 +/- 0.0119    
  2             +10.5 +/-   5.4 Hz       +13.6 +/-   5.3 Hz      +0.0518 +/- 0.0110    
  3              -0.3 +/-   3.7 Hz        -2.3 +/-   4.4 Hz      +0.0745 +/- 0.0105    
  4              +0.5 +/-   3.1 Hz        -2.1 +/-   3.3 Hz      +0.0445 +/- 0.0104    

  WHAT EACH STEP KEEPS   ratio of sums, jackknife SE over 18 chains
    generation 1 / 0   +0.266 +/- 0.084
    generation 2 / 1   +0.409 +/- 0.157
    generation 3 / 2   (denominator not resolved: generation 2 is +10.5 +/- 5.4 Hz)
    generation 4 / 3   (denominator not resolved: generation 3 is -0.3 +/- 3.7 Hz)

  THE ALTERNATION TEST   predicted signs for generations 1-4 are -, +, -, +
    mean of (predicted sign x dF1)   +10.4 +/- 3.9 Hz  (2.7 SE)
  positive means the flipped chain inverts its convention at every step,
  which only happens if each generation is reading its tutor's mapping.

  DID THE LAST LESSON LAND   generation 4:  +0.0445 +/- 0.0104  (4.3 SE)

  IT DECAYS. Generation 4 is within 3 SE of zero (+0.5 +/- 3.1 Hz),
  so the convention does not survive the chain: each pupil hands on less
  than it received until nothing is left. Culture STARTS here and does not
  ACCUMULATE -- the opposite of what human iterated learning does, where
  structure increases down the chain.

  WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT LICENSE. It does not say the channel is
  lossy: `tutor` left open whether anything is lost beyond the WIDTH of
  what a tutor says, at 2.6 and 2.8 SE, and a decaying series is exactly
  what a width-limited channel produces as well. Distinguishing them needs
  a generation taught from a WIDENED tape, which is the `loud` arm run
  down a chain rather than once.
